 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "offers rows are [offerId, startAt, endAt, maxCount] and events rows are [userId, timestamp, action, offerId] with decimal-string numbers; action is \"redeem\" or \"unredeem\". Process events in input order. An event takes effect only if its offer exists, startAt <= timestamp <= endAt and timestamp <= processingTime. A redeem raises the user's count for that offer when the count is below maxCount (otherwise it is ignored); an unredeem lowers a positive count. Return [userId, offerIds] for every user that appears in events, sorted by userId in code-point order, where offerIds lists (in offers order) the offers with startAt <= processingTime <= endAt whose count for that user is below maxCount.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk06-a-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
